   =\Bigl(\sum_{i=1}^{2025}(2i-1)x_i\Bigr)
     \Bigl(\sum_{i=1}^{2025}\frac{x_i}{2i-1}\Bigr).
\]

Denote  

\[
A=\sum_{i}(2i-1)x_i,\qquad B=\sum_{i}\frac{x_i}{2i-1},
\]
so that \(F=A\,B\).

The vector \((A,B)\) is a convex combination of the points  

\[
P_i=\bigl(2i-1,\; \frac1{2i-1}\bigr),\qquad i=1,\dots ,2025 .
\]

All \(P_i\) lie on the hyperbola \(xy=1\); the function \(y=1/x\) is convex for \(x>0\).  
