        \[
f(n)=\max_{a_i\in[-1,1]}\sum_{i=1}^n\Bigl|\frac{S-a_i}{n}-a_i\Bigr|
      =\frac1n\max_{a_i\in[-1,1]}\sum_{i=1}^n\bigl|S-(n+1)a_i\bigr|
\]

The function inside the maximum is a sum of absolute values, i.e. a convex
piecewise‑linear function of the variables \(a_i\).
Hence its maximum over the hyper‑cube \([-1,1]^n\) is attained at a vertex,
so each \(a_i\) can be taken to be \(\pm1\).

Let \(m\) be the number of indices with \(a_i=1\) \((0\le m\le n)\).
Then \(S=2m-n\) and

\[
\sum_{i=1}^n\bigl|S-(n+1)a_i\bigr|
 =m\bigl|S-(n+1)\bigr|+(n-m)\bigl|S+(n+1)\bigr|
 =n+4m(n-m).
\]

Thus

\[
f(n)=\frac{1}{n}\bigl(n+4\max_{0\le m\le n}m(n-m)\bigr)
     =1+\frac{4}{n}\Bigl\lfloor\frac n2\Bigr\rfloor
                \Bigl\lceil\frac n2\Bigr\rceil .
\]

Consequently  

\[
f(n)=\begin{cases}
n+1, & n\text{ even},\\[2mm]
n+1-\dfrac1n, & n\text{ odd}.
\end{cases}
\]

Now

\[
\sum_{k=1}^{225}k\,f(k)
   =\sum_{k=1}^{225}k(k+1)-\sum_{\substack{k\le225\\k\text{ odd}}}1
   =\frac{225\cdot226\cdot227}{3}-113.
\]

Since \(225\cdot226\cdot227/3=3\,847\,650\) and there are \((225+1)/2=113\) odd
integers in \([1,225]\),

\[
\boxed{3\,847\,537}.
\]

