\qquad\text{(matrix determinant lemma)} .
\]

Take  

\[
D=\operatorname{diag}\bigl(i^{3}-i\bigr)_{i=2}^{n},
\qquad 
u=v=-\lambda\mathbf 1 .
\]

Since \(i^{3}-i=i(i-1)(i+1)\neq0\) for \(i\ge2\), \(D\) is invertible and

\[
